speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, the House will recall an announcement by the Minister of Transport some days ago proposing that ihe question of ground transportation at airports in Canada should be the subject matter of a committee study. There has now been consultation with the representatives of the various parties and I believe there might be unanimous consent to an order in the following terms:
That the Standing Committee on Transport and Communications be directed to examine the subject matter of ground transportation at airports in Canada;
And that during its consideration of the aforementioned matter the committee be empowered to adjourn from place to place within Canada.
